    <subfield code="a">"Bruno Schulz, the Polish author born in 1892, wrote fantastical tales about his life, town and family. This book takes those stories as its starting point. As a tale progresses, its content overwhelms the page, so birds burst forth from letters, words melt, and typographies collide and move on: Bruno's tragic life become woven into the tales he wrote." -- [foreword by] Peter Duffin.</subfield>
